.TH SDL_utf8strlcpy 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_utf8strlcpy \- Copy an UTF-8 string.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t SDL_utf8strlcpy(char *dst, const char *src, size_t dst_bytes);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function copies up to
.BR dst_bytes
- 1 bytes from
.BR src
to
.BR dst
while also ensuring that the string written to
.BR dst
does not end in a truncated multi-byte sequence\[char46] Finally, it appends a null terminator\[char46]
.PP
.BR src
and
.BR dst
must not overlap\[char46]
.PP
Note that unlike
.BR SDL_strlcpy (),
this function returns the number of bytes written, not the length of
.BR src \[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I dst
The destination buffer\[char46] Must not be NULL, and must not overlap with
.BR src \[char46]

.TP
.I src
The null-terminated UTF-8 string to copy\[char46] Must not be NULL, and must not overlap with
.BR dst \[char46]

.TP
.I dst_bytes
The length (in bytes) of the destination buffer\[char46] Must not be 0\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes written, excluding the null terminator\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_strlcpy (3)
